1218: def _align_pair_landmark_aware(o: Track, i: Track, policy=None) -> Alignment:
1219:     """Pair a named incoming ownership point with outgoing section/dropout cuts.
1220: 
1221:     Default policy: the earliest incoming DROP that yields a valid 16-48 bar
1222:     blend wins. This prevents a later drop from gaming the score while still
1223:     allowing a second drop when the first would force an immediate bass swap
1224:     (Fresh Mix T1).
1225: 
1226:     `allow_intro_phrase_swaps` adds interior intro phrase points as a RESCUE
1227:     pass, tried only when no drop anchor yields a valid blend. That ordering is
1228:     deliberate. Pooling intro and drop anchors together and ranking them was
1229:     measured against the correction mix and moved T3 from bar 24 - which the
1230:     default already gets right, matching Sam - to bar 16. Reproducing Sam's
1231:     earlier T4/T5 swaps needs a selection rule that distinguishes "wait for the
1232:     drop after a 24-bar intro" from "take the midpoint of a 32-bar intro", and
