 915: #: Hard floor for _outgoing_has_post_swap_content's "genuinely nothing left"
 916: #: read - matches the existing QUICK_SWAP margin, so a swap that clears this
 917: #: floor can already produce a valid (if abrupt) handoff (Rule 1's own
 918: #: boundary-margin test already pins that anything tighter is a hard error).
 919: MIN_REMAINING_CONTENT_BARS = 1.0
 920: 
 921: 
 922: def _outgoing_has_post_swap_content(o: Track, swap_bar: float,
 923:                                     effective_end: float | None = None) -> bool:
 924:     """True iff the outgoing still has real content to fade across after
 925:     *swap_bar* (the outgoing's OWN native bar the handoff lands on) - false
 926:     means this is a genuine cold ending, not a defect to correct.
 927: 
 928:     Sam, 2026-09-12 (correcting apply_automation's fixed margin rule):
 929:     "sometimes the outgoing track can run all the way up to the drop of the
 930:     next track... so it could plausibly happen within [a few bars] of the
 931:     end of the track" - a swap sitting close to the overlap's end is not
 932:     automatically wrong; it depends on whether the outgoing actually has
 933:     anything left to give at that point.
 934: 
 935:     Distance to *effective_end* (defaults to the track's own real end,
 936:     `n_bars`) alone: regardless of what's still playing, there's no time
 937:     left to fade through once the swap is within MIN_REMAINING_CONTENT_BARS
 938:     of it. Pass an explicit `effective_end` when an outgoing-tail loop has
 939:     extended playback past the native end (see the compute_aligned_positions
 940:     call site, which does this AFTER plan_fill_or_cut runs) - a loop only
 941:     ever adds content, so the caller should never pass something SMALLER
 942:     than `o.n_bars` here.
 943: 
 944:     `bass_out_is_end` was tried and DROPPED as a second signal (Codex
 945:     review, 2026-09-13): it only means the bass specifically never returns
 946:     before the file ends, not that every stem has - Christoph, The Rise
 947:     (n_bars=256, bass-out~253, drums-only outro through 256) has 3 real
 948:     bars of percussion after its bass-out point, which the bass signal
 949:     alone would have misread as a cold ending. Bass ownership is not
 950:     sufficient evidence of "nothing left" - only actual distance to the
 951:     track's end is checked now.
 952:     """
 953:     end = o.n_bars if effective_end is None else effective_end
 954:     return (end - swap_bar) > MIN_REMAINING_CONTENT_BARS
 955: 
